<channel|>We talk a lot about the "smart home" revolution, but we rarely discuss the accessibility gap in home energy dashboards. Most interfaces rely heavily on complex line graphs, color-coded heat maps, and real-time data visualizations to convey usage patterns. 

While intuitive for many, these designs create significant barriers for neurodivergent users or those with visual impairments. If our transition to a green grid depends on consumer data, we must ensure that the tools used to manage it are designed for everyone, not just the visually able. [end of text]


